{"id": "EUVD-2026-80549", "enisaUuid": "35dce4f0-fe42-3543-bb41-291adfd5065d", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbatman-adv: dat: avoid unaligned fault in IP extraction\n\nIndependent of the alignment of the ARP packet in the SKB, either the\nbatadv_arp_ip_src or the batadv_arp_ip_dst will have an unaligned access\n(on HW without native unaligned read support).\n\nUse get_unaligned() to handle this properly on all architectures.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T10:32:34", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:55:23", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b1bbc694ca51adb8dbed3f3235b4fcbdb44e0e20", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/15dbfb37f0e1a085d48deeb8f5238e9d28127dde", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a170d4617e8cca05a1314de61728a262ef272782", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c74a4acf41d19f21199dec2d6c813c90d31cd02c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/91c99b4e152023c7d458a5dedd52d2b0d7df4ce3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1cfa7d5f70d54cb8c7e82df739430782d1996ee1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0c2df865338bbf92aa45b9253e5f9b8ef2d9992f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0121afa52cdb88cfb4d5d7bd126a23a9100121d8"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89949", "GHSA-95x9-5832-jchc"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "05e01daa-2892-3985-906f-364ec8b89caa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.221"}, {"id": "15c26223-1ee5-3754-998a-0a59cec5e74e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5c3a0e5535933349a5d6e6bc8b704e0611f21d3f <1cfa7d5f70d54cb8c7e82df739430782d1996ee1"}, {"id": "2000c1b3-fea2-378f-96b5-0c6ba1151b2a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5c3a0e5535933349a5d6e6bc8b704e0611f21d3f <15dbfb37f0e1a085d48deeb8f5238e9d28127dde"}, {"id": "20903b3b-aba1-3f3e-b80b-805858899764", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_